  <h2>The question we answer</h2>
  <p>Where should I go if the ocean experience matters as much as the luxury of the holiday? Most travel sites answer half of that question. Surf publications focus on waves; dive sites focus on reefs; luxury travel media focuses on hotels. We bring the three together — and we always start with the water.</p>

  <h2>Who we write for</h2>
  <p>Our primary readers are European travellers — from the UK, Germany, France, Spain, Italy, the Netherlands, Belgium, Switzerland, Austria and Scandinavia — planning premium surf, dive, freedive and ocean-focused holidays. That shapes how we write: seasons framed around the European calendar, honest discussion of long-haul versus short-haul, and planning advice that respects limited holiday time.</p>

  <h2>How we work</h2>
  <p>Surf and Dive is written and maintained by the <strong>Surf and Dive Editorial Team</strong>. Our guides are built from official tourism-board information, recognised surf, dive and freediving organisations and established travel sources, combined with editorial judgement about who each destination suits.</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>We do not fabricate first-hand experience.</strong> We do not claim to have surfed a break, dived a reef or stayed in a resort unless that is genuinely true, and we say so when it is.</li>
    <li><strong>We do not invent facts.</strong> No made-up prices, flight times, availability, awards, partnerships, reviews or testimonials.</li>
    <li><strong>We qualify seasonal information.</strong> Conditions are described as typical patterns, never guarantees.</li>
    <li><strong>Scores are editorial.</strong> Our 1–10 scores for surf, diving, freediving, luxury and scenery are positioning scores to help comparison, not objective rankings.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Read our full <a href="/editorial-standards/">editorial standards</a>, our <a href="/responsible-travel/">responsible travel principles</a> and our <a href="/ocean-safety/">approach to ocean safety</a>.</p>

  <h2>Independence</h2>
  <p>Surf and Dive is an editorial discovery platform, not a booking engine. We do not currently sell holidays or accept payment for inclusion. If that ever changes — for example through affiliate links or partnerships — we will disclose it clearly on every affected page.</p>

  <h2>Get in touch</h2>
  <p>Corrections, updates and editorial questions are welcome. <a href="/contact/">Contact the editorial team</a>.</p>
